' plan-115-A: ISOLATED is orthogonal to visibility. A PRIVATE ISOLATED FUNC is
' a well-formed declaration and builds clean.
'
' This fixture replaces bug227_private_isolated_func_invalid, which pinned the
' opposite. bug-227's rationale was "an ISOLATED function is a thread entry
' point, reached by name from another package's thread::start, so it must be
' project-visible" -- and plan-115-A deletes exactly that reachability
' requirement, leaving the visibility half with no justification. The
' declaration-form half of TYPE_ISOLATED_NOT_VISIBLE still stands and is pinned
' by the sibling fixture isolated_sub_invalid.
PRIVATE ISOLATED FUNC w(x AS Integer) AS Integer
  RETURN x
END FUNC

' PUBLIC (the default) and EXPORT were already accepted; PRIVATE is the one this
' plan adds. Declared alongside so the fixture pins that widening the rule did
' not narrow anything else.
PUBLIC ISOLATED FUNC pub(x AS Integer) AS Integer
  RETURN x
END FUNC

FUNC main AS Integer
  RETURN 0
END FUNC
